{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PROVENANCE ORACLE CONFIRMED LIVE, AND THE PRE-CUTOVER BASELINE CAPTURED. This de-risks the vote criterion: its prerequisite [rebar:e951-7df6-1851-4d5e] is not merely 'landed', it is demonstrably STAMPING in production, so a null provenance after the cutover would mean the cutover, not a broken oracle.\n\nWHERE THE EVIDENCE LIVES, recorded because I had to work it out and the next person should not. The code_review artifact ticket's description is only a one-line summary; the payload is a SIDECAR EVENT FILE in the ticket's store directory, named '<ts>-<uuid>-REVIEW_RESULT.json' (the event type is REVIEW_RESULT, NOT 'code_review' — globbing for the latter finds nothing). Artifacts are titled 'code-review: <Change-Id> @ <revision-sha>', so they are findable by Change-Id via 'rebar list --type=code_review --sort=-created'. Note that command's real interface: 'list' takes NEITHER --limit NOR -o json (it emits JSON already, and has --output llm); passing '--limit=N -o json' produces EMPTY OUTPUT rather than an error, which silently looks like 'no artifacts exist'. There are 855 of them.\n\nBASELINE, from the newest artifact at the time of writing — code-review: I47ff3bbd2a0e5cac443508a3e3a1cdf83faf4057 @ 70370adf6, created 1785797887630491367, i.e. AFTER e951 landed as a601ae0fd2:\n\n    data.provider_provenance = {\n      \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n      \"model\": \"anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6\",\n      \"tier\": \"first_class\",\n      \"endpoint_host\": null,\n      \"capabilities\": {\"prompt_cache_style\": \"anthropic\", \"native_structured_output\": false,\n                       \"supports_temperature\": true, \"supports_thinking\": true}\n    }\n    data.model = \"claude-opus-4-8\"\n\nThree things follow.\n1. The field is POPULATED, not None. Before e951, code_review/finalize.py set 'model' and nothing set 'provenance', so sidecar.py's read returned None. It no longer does. The criterion's prerequisite is satisfied by OBSERVATION rather than by the merge commit existing.\n2. THE EXACT POST-CUTOVER EXPECTATION IS NOW UNAMBIGUOUS: this same field must read provider == 'bedrock' with model == 'bedrock:us.anthropic.*', and 'capabilities.prompt_cache_style' should move off 'anthropic' to the Bedrock style. I will compare the same key on the same artifact shape rather than eyeballing a log line.\n3. An adjacent observation worth carrying rather than tripping over later: data.model is 'claude-opus-4-8' while data.provider_provenance.model is 'anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6'. These are NOT contradictory — per finalize.py:241 the provenance is taken from the VERIFY step (_verify_step_provenance), which resolves the STANDARD class, while the top-level model names the frontier pass. So the two fields are the per-pass split showing through, and post-cutover I expect opus on the top-level field and sonnet in the provenance, both bedrock:-qualified. Anyone reading only one of the two fields would draw the wrong conclusion about which class was used."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785798405167705001,"uuid":"5dc4af3c-6812-456d-a1fb-e230110fe30d"}